      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In studying the pathogenesis of acute gastric and duodenal ulcers arising in operated patients against the background of purulent-septic complications, the specific signs distinguishing them from stress-ulcers, which develop in response to surgical aggression, were revealed. They are: the absence of inflammatory reaction in the gastric mucosa, its ischemia, hypo- and achlorhydria with reduction in the proteolytic activity of gastric juice."},
